 ## 🔥 Git Safety Protocol (CRITICAL)
 
+### 🚨 **ABSOLUTELY NEVER RUN THESE COMMANDS** 🚨
+
+```bash
+# ❌❌❌ FORBIDDEN - DESTROYS SUBMODULE BRANCHES ❌❌❌
+git submodule update          # PUTS SUBMODULES IN DETACHED HEAD!!!
+git submodule update --init   # DESTROYS BRANCH STATE!!!  
+git submodule update --recursive  # CATASTROPHIC!!!
+
+# ❌❌❌ THESE COMMANDS BREAK EVERYTHING ❌❌❌
+# NEVER EVER USE THESE - THEY RESET SUBMODULES TO COMMIT HASHES
+# INSTEAD OF KEEPING THEM ON BRANCHES!!!
+```
+
+### ✅ **CORRECT Way to Fix Detached HEAD Submodules**
+
+When submodules get put into detached HEAD (because someone ran the forbidden commands above):
+
+```bash
+# Fix each submodule individually - go into each directory
+cd packages/haive-mcp
+git checkout feature/fix_everything
+cd ../haive-prebuilt
+git checkout feature/fix_everything  
+cd ../haive-dataflow
+git checkout feature/fix_everything
+cd ../haive-tools
+git checkout feature/fix_everything
+cd ../haive-core
+git checkout feature/fix_everything
+cd ../haive-agents
+git checkout feature/fix_everything
+cd ../../  # Back to root
+
+# THEN commit the submodule reference updates from root
+git add packages/haive-mcp packages/haive-prebuilt packages/haive-dataflow packages/haive-tools packages/haive-core packages/haive-agents
+git commit -m "fix: restore submodules to feature/fix_everything branches"
+```
+
